9. Why MLP Before GRU

A GRU-based language model was also considered.

However, for the current stage, an MLP is the better experimental choice.

The main reason is that the goal is not yet to build the final language encoder. The immediate question is:

"How predictable is the learned action representation 
𝑧
𝐴
 from language?"

Using a relatively simple language representation and MLP makes this question easier to answer.

If the MLP performs reasonably well, a GRU or stronger sequence encoder can subsequently be tested to determine whether the limitation comes from language encoding capacity.

If the MLP already performs poorly, increasing model complexity may simply increase overfitting without solving the underlying data limitation.

