The resulting performance will serve as the primary baseline for determining whether the learned action latent is meaningfully predictable from language.

After this baseline is established, experiments with different latent dimensions (8/16/32/64) and eventually sequence-based language encoders such as GRUs can determine whether improvements come from a better latent representation, a better language encoder, or simply increased model capacity.

The central research question at this stage is therefore:

How much of the action representation learned purely from behavior can be recovered from language alone?

This provides a clean foundation for the subsequent development of the full AntVLA architecture.
